# Breadcrumbs

Publishing breadcrumbs expose the parent hierarchy of an information page. They are navigation, not transaction progress. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/breadcrumbs/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use a short hierarchy when a person can arrive directly at a device guide or a nested documentation page. Link the real parent area and its collection. A dashboard already oriented by its sidebar and room title may not need another trail.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a named navigation landmark and an ordered list. Keep each parent label consistent with its destination title. If the current page is shown, use plain text or aria-current="page". Decorative separators must not be read as extra content. The local site shell remains the owner of the primary breadcrumb implementation.

## Home Assistant boundary

A breadcrumb does not describe browser history. Do not manufacture a parent route from a dashboard URL, assume that every entity belongs to one room, or copy a government topic taxonomy into Home Assistant.

